messages:
maria: dropped a wobble-y prototype for the compact capacity row. the idea: allow drag-to-adjust on the min/max handles in the table row. figma link: https://www.figma.com/file/zzz/compact-capacity-gesture. Quick take needed: gesture discoverability, copy, and how burst fits inline.

samir: Nice concept. Two implementation flags: 1) drag gesture needs a clear affordance (maybe a grab icon). 2) we'll need to debounce network saves when people drag quickly. also mobile touch friction might be weird.

kelly: microcopy: current placeholder "Min GPUs" and "Max GPUs" is fine but the helper under the row should explain the impact: "Min keeps warm instances to meet latency SLOs". For burst label, I prefer "Burst (ephemeral)" vs "On-demand burst". I'll test both.

aj (PM): +1 to the helper. Also policy note: if min > 0 we should auto-disable cold-start grace. Need product confirmation from ryan on metrics impact.

ryan (Data): If we set default min=1 for 'latency' pools we see a ~12% increase in baseline cost but 30% fewer p95 latency spikes in our experiments. I can add a small chart to the design notes showing cost vs p95 tradeoff.

zoe (A11y): Accessibility: draggable handles must support keyboard alternatives: arrow keys to increment/decrement, page up/down for larger steps. Announce changes with aria-live polite: "Min GPUs changed to 3". Also ensure the grab icon has aria-hidden and the control itself is the interactive element. Contrast note: the drag handle outline is too faint at 14px size.

samir (FE): snippet for keyboard handling I'll add to the PR: 

```js
// pseudo
handle.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === 'ArrowUp') setValue(v+1);
  if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft' || e.key === 'ArrowDown') setValue(v-1);
  if (e.key === 'PageUp') setValue(Math.min(max, v+10));
  if (e.key === 'PageDown') setValue(Math.max(min, v-10));
});

// announce
const live = document.getElementById('capacity-live');
live.textContent = `Min GPUs changed to ${value}`; // aria-live="polite"
```

samir: also we should prevent accidental drag when users try to select number text; maybe require a 6px horizontal move before starting drag.

maria: good call. On the burst placement: earlier we had it as a pill right of the max input, but in compact rows that pushes overflow. Proposed alternative: put a subtle icon between the pool name and min/max that opens a small popover with burst toggle and estimate. That keeps the row tight. Thoughts?

kelly: Popover makes sense for dense tables. Ensure the popover is keyboard and screen-reader accessible (focus trap? probably focus should go into popover on open and return on close). Copy inside: "Enable burst to temporarily exceed max for short peaks." Short and scannable.

aj (PM): Popover ok but we need a visual indicator on the row when burst is enabled: a small green dot + text "+burst" so people can scan table. Also the cost preview should be available in hover/tooltip.

zoe (A11y): For the popover: do not use role=dialog for tiny tooltips; role=menu or a plain popup with aria-expanded on trigger is fine. If it's interactive (has toggles), it must be a dialog-like component but keep it lightweight. Add aria-labels for the burst toggle.

ryan (Data): Add a tiny inline sparkline next to pool name showing typical hourly utilization; helps decide min/max. Could be optional. Small perf cost but valuable for power users.

maria: I like sparkline. For mobile we'll hide sparks. Also update copy: replace "Max" label with "Max (reserved)" to clarify burst is separate.

kelly: I'll update the Figma frames: a) table with inline burst pill b) table with popover trigger c) dense mobile collapse. I'll include the two copy variants and mark which are A/B candidates.

samir: Implementation notes: I'll do keyboard interactions + 6px drag threshold + debounce saves. For the popover I'll reuse existing small-popover component and add focus-return.

deploybot (bot): Preview build for branch compact-capacity-gesture queued  build id: 98765  preview: https://preview.redwood.work/compact-capacity-gesture (ETA ~20m).

maria: Action items: kelly update mocks and A/B variants; samir prototype keyboard/drag heuristics in demo; zoe write accessibility checklist for popover and drag handles; ryan produce cost vs latency chart to attach. We'll reconvene tomorrow for a run-through. Thanks! :rocket:
